# Default: normalise text in the repo, check out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVIDENCE — byte-exact, never transformed.
#
# `make verify` SHA-256s the stored CAQM order bytes and matches cited quotes
# verbatim against the extracted page text. If Git rewrote line endings on
# checkout, a judge cloning this repo on a different OS would get different
# bytes than we hashed, and verification would fail for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the citations. `-text` disables all conversion.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
corpus/sources/** -text
*.pdf binary

# Keep Makefile tabs and shell scripts LF regardless of platform.
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Don't count vendored or research material in language stats.
docs/research/** linguist-documentation
